The  program communicates with the Advanced Power Management dae‐
mon, making requests of the current power status or  placing  the
system  either  into suspend or stand‐by state.  The tool is only
installed on supported platforms.  With no  flags,  displays  the
current  power  management state in verbose form.  Available com‐
mand‐line flags are: Display the external charger  (A/C  status):
0  means  disconnected,  1  means connected, 2 means backup power
source, and 255 means unknown.  Display  the  battery  status:  0
means  high,  1  means low, 2 means critical, 3 means charging, 4
means absent, and 255 means unknown.  Do not communicate with the
